MEPs postponed the vote on the bill last month until it is analyzed by a mixed parliamentary commission.
On Wednesday, MEPs applauaded the proposal, after which the Senate did so again.
According to the new legislative regulation, there should be a criminal abortion in three cases: if a woman's life is at risk if the fetus has no chance of survival, or if the pregnancy originated from rape.
Similar exceptions have existed in Chile since 1931, even before women were given the right to suffrage there in 1949.
