Pruitt, who before joining the role of the head of the EPA by President-elect Donald Trump, served for a long time a reliably an opponent of stricter environmental regulations.
Since it settled in Washington, Pruitt has repeatedly shifted or delayed the regulations proposed by the chemical and fossil industries.
Sudden Wednesday's turnaround is the greatest legal failure for Pruitta's regulatory agenda.
