"The turnaround in the views of the EPA - following our judicial over - is an important victor for the health and safety of those 6.7 million New Yorkers and more than 115 million Americans who are directly affected by air pollution," Schneiderman said.
New York was joined by California, Connecticut, Delaware, Illinois, Iowa, Maine, Massachusetts, Minnesota, New Mexico, Oregon, Pensylvania, Rhode Island, Vermont, Washington and Washington, D.C.
Substantive ozone arises when ordinary harmful substances emitted by cars, power plants, oil refineries, chemical power plants and other sources react in an atmosphere with solar radiation.
Responsible smog can cause serious respiratory problems in sensitive people and thousands of premature deaths every year.
Advocate public health defenders and environmentalists acknowledge Pruitta's sudden change with gratitude.
“It’s troubling about the coercion needs to execute in order to change the mindset of those responsible and to protect the air we’re breathing,” said Lori Ann Burd of the Biological Diversity Center.
