Suicide bomber attacked a military convoy in Kabul's capital of Afghanistan. One NATO soldier died in the attack and several others were injured, officials said.
Injured were five soldiers and an interpreter, according to a NATO statement.
Unofficial reports also killed three civilians.
This month, a bomb attack struck Afghanistan - on Tuesday, more than 30 people were killed in an explosion at a Heratian mosque.
On Monday, a suicidal assailant killed two people near an Iraqi embassies in Kabul.
In a statement, NATO said Tuesday's explosion occurred after the patrol, along with the members of the Afghan army, was attacked by a "local person with home-provoked explosive devices."
The statement further states that all wounded soldiers are out of danger to their lives and they are located in a U.S. military hospital at Bagram air base.
According to correspondents, the increasing power of the Taliban and a group known as the Islamic State (IS) in Qarabagh is an important source of concern for NATO allied forces in nearby Bagram.
