At the end of July, a bomb placed in a car killed at least 30 people in Kabul's Shia district.
The Taliban claimed responsibility for the attack.
On May 31, a large explosion in the city center was killed by more than 150 people. This is the country's deadest militant attack since U.S. troops overthrew the Taliban government in 2001.
Violence is undermining an already dubious situation in Afghanistan, and U.S. President Donald Trump is considering an increase in U.S. troops who should be assisting military units and police officers in the country.
