The young couple vanished without a trace 12 years ago.
Their car has now been found at the bottom of the Volcano.
A pair of young Russian Ilya Zirnov and Kira Cherkasova have been missing since December 2005.
Extensive quivering was rampant, but without success.
Finally, due to a lack of evidence, the police terminated the investigation.
Families of the missing couple lived in the insecurities not to learn what had happened to the couple.
After 12 years came the sad ending of the whole story.
The wreck of their car was found by a lay-smart diver at the bottom of the Volga River in the town of Čeboksara in Čuvaš.
It wasn't only thanks to the documents that remained in the car, the police managed to identify the couple.
Procedoors have survived underwater for a decade, without which it would take the police much longer to find out the identities of those found much longer.
