"You're inferior than me," Trump joked.
Suddenly the tone exacerbtized the tone of the conversation.
"I hate accepting these people," Trump remarked.
Assume that they're bad.
That's why they're in jail right now.
"They won't be great people to go to work for local dairy farmers," he said.
In an interview, he also pointed out that a fugitive could become a Boston bomber in five years.
At the end of January, about a week after arriving at the White House, Trump conducted telephone conversations with a number of world leaders, often several in one day.
In the end, the conversation with Turnbul described as the least enjoyable for the whole day.
Before he finished it, he pointed out that he previously had a pleasant conversation with Russian President Vladimir Putin.
