The hot and droughy weather of the last few days resulted in an increased number of fires.
On Tuesday, firefighters in the whole of the Czech Republic eliminated 108 of them, i.e. twice the long-term daily average.
On Tuesday during the day when temperatures in the Czech Republic climbed more than 35 degrees Celsius, firefighters were mainly engaged in the fight against the blaze.
"Fires in the natural environment predominate, as well as those associated with harvest work," fire department spokeswoman Nicole Zaoral said.
There was no relief for firefighters in an evening change of the weather, when the heat in many places was replaced by thunderstorms and torrent collisions.
