Italians toughen up to fight NGO rescue ships with immigrants on board
Italy has announced that it will prevent the arrival of NGO rescue ships arriving on the coast of Italy with immigrants from the Mediterranean unless the NGO signs new rules regulating their operations.
“Unavailated if the NGO doesn’t sign up the new rules of conduct, it’s hard for us that they could continue their operations,” Interior Minister Marco Minniti said in an interview with Turin daily La Stampa.
Minniti's warning came a day after Italian authorities seized the German bailing organization Jugend Rettet on suspicion of human trafficking, which greatly facilitates illegal immigration.
The bailout organization, which operates for the first year, declined to comment on the matter due to the allegations by Italian prosecutor Ambrogio Cartosio.
