Lavender of Provence Threaten Climate Change
Lavender has become a symbol of Provence in south-eastern France, but are now threatened by climate change.
The lavender is declining due to dry climates and harmful insects, which provokes dismay on the faces of researchers and farmers who are looking for a solution.
Eric Chaises, an expert of the CIEPPAM agricultural research institute in Provence, said: "Growing lavender in Provence is at risk because in the last few years this plant has been subjected to climate change, which brings with it less rainfall in spring and autumn.
This Affects Lavender Life.
Cyccades and loungers carrying micro-Bacteria who thrive in a dry climite are also to blame.”
